# Siraj (سراج) — Parallel Implementation Plan & Architecture (Hackathon MVP)

This document outlines the parallelized architecture and implementation plan for building **Siraj (سراج)**, a smart financial assistant. The plan is structured into three parts:
1. **Frontend (FE) Implementation** (with mock data fallbacks for independent development)
2. **Backend (BE) & AI Agent Implementation**
3. **Integration Phase**

---

## 🏗️ 1. Parallel Development Architecture

To support parallel development, the frontend and backend are decoupled using a clear interface contract. The frontend client will contain a toggle to switch between a local Mock API client and the actual HTTP/SSE backend client.

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph Frontend [React Frontend - RTL Cairo Font]
        UI[UI Components & Pages] --> ClientAdapter{Client Adapter}
        ClientAdapter -->|Mock Toggle = True| MockAPI[Mock Client / In-memory Data]
        ClientAdapter -->|Mock Toggle = False| RealAPI[Axios API Client / EventSource]
    end

    subgraph Backend [FastAPI Backend]
        RealAPI -->|REST / SSE HTTP| Router[FastAPI Routers]
        Router --> ORM[SQLAlchemy / SQLModel]
        ORM --> DB[(SQLite DB)]
        Router --> AI[Gemini AI Agent]
        AI <-->|Function Calling| Tools[15 Financial Tools]
        Tools --> ORM
    end
```

