## 🔄 Part 3: Integration Plan

Once FE and BE are complete, they are integrated by configuring the frontend to talk to the API.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant FE as React Frontend
    participant BE as FastAPI Backend
    participant GEM as Google Gemini API

    Note over FE,BE: Integration Test Phase
    FE->>FE: Toggle MOCK_API = false
    FE->>BE: POST /api/v1/auth/login
    BE-->>FE: JWT Token

    FE->>BE: GET /api/v1/dashboard/overview (with Auth Header)
    BE-->>FE: Return aggregated 3-year data

    Note over FE,GEM: AI Agent Integration
    FE->>BE: POST /api/v1/chat/sessions/1/messages ("أضف 50 ريال قهوة")
    BE->>GEM: System Prompt + Context + Message
    GEM-->>BE: Tool Call: add_transaction(amount=50, category='مطاعم ومقاهي')
    BE->>BE: Insert to SQLite
    BE->>GEM: Tool Result: Success
    GEM-->>BE: Text: "أبشر، أضفت 50 ريال لمصروفات القهوة."
    BE-->>FE: Stream: "أبشر، أضفت..." (SSE)
    FE->>FE: Refresh dashboard charts automatically
```

### Integration Steps
1. **CORS Configuration**: Configure FastAPI to allow connections from the Vite dev server port.
2. **Environment Synchronization**: Point the frontend `.env` to the FastAPI backend host URL.
3. **Authentication Handshake**: Replace the Mock auth hook with local storage storage of JWT and Axios interceptors to attach `Authorization: Bearer <token>` to all backend requests.
4. **Chat Stream Hook**: Connect the chat bubble UI to a native JS `EventSource` or `fetch-reader` stream targeting the FastAPI SSE endpoint to display tokens in real-time.
5. **Event-Driven UI Refresh**: Implement a dashboard refresh mechanism that re-triggers data fetching whenever Siraj executes a data-altering tool (such as adding transactions or setting budgets).
